# What the `note` grammar reads a scope's text to (note/term/mill/03-note-grammar.md): one expression, as a tree of
# these nodes. Every node carries `at`, the code point in the scope's text where it begins, so a mistake found later
# (a unit, an operator nothing lowers) is reported where it was written.

load @term/base/unit
  find unit-entry

# one factor of a quantity's unit: `s` to -2 in `m/s^2`, with the registered unit it names
form unit-factor
  link entry, like unit-entry
  link power, like number

form note-node
  mark tag, name kind
  # `42`, `3.14`, `0xff`, `1e-9`. `literal` is the number as Term writes it: `1e-9` is `0.000000001`
  case number-node
    link at, like number
    link literal, like text
    link decimal, like boolean
  # a number and a registered unit: `9.81m/s^2`, `20MB/s`, `$20`. `value` is a decimal literal, `unit` the unit as
  # written (a currency by its code), and `factors` what each part of it names
  case quantity-node
    link at, like number
    link value, like text
    link unit, like text
    link factors, like list, like unit-factor
  # `"text"`, its escapes read
  case text-node
    link at, like number
    link value, like text
  case name-node
    link at, like number
    link name, like text
  # `-x`, `not x`. The operator in its one spelling: `-`, `+`, `not`
  case unary-node
    link at, like number
    link operator, like text
    link operand, like note-node
  # `x + y`. The operator in its one spelling: `≤` is `<=`, `==` is `=`, `&&` is `and`, `×` is `*`
  case binary-node
    link at, like number
    link operator, like text
    link left, like note-node
    link right, like note-node
  # `sin(x)`, `a.b(x)`
  case call-node
    link at, like number
    link callee, like note-node
    link arguments, like list, like note-node
  # `x[4]`
  case index-node
    link at, like number
    link target, like note-node
    link index, like note-node
  # `foo.bar`
  case member-node
    link at, like number
    link target, like note-node
    link name, like text
  # `[1, 2, 3]`
  case list-node
    link at, like number
    link items, like list, like note-node
  # `{x, y, z}`
  case set-node
    link at, like number
    link items, like list, like note-node
  # `1..10` (both ends in), `0..<100` (the end out), and the intervals `[0, 1)`, `(0, 1]`, `(0, 1)`
  case range-node
    link at, like number
    link from, like note-node
    link to, like note-node
    link from-open, like boolean
    link to-open, like boolean

# a mistake in a scope's text, at the code point `at`
form note-problem
  link at, like number
  link message, like text
  link hint, like text

# what reading gives: the expression, or none and the first mistake that stopped it
form note-read
  link node, like maybe, like note-node
  link problems, like list, like note-problem
